## Summary

The owner (29 Oct) said "i really cant stand this setup screen". They approved the mockup (https://claude.ai/artifact/L2LRmYRCs7nn4g5pz3FHLA, "build the setup redesign"), then chose "Hide it when done", and then asked: "don't have [Setup] show back up once i unplug my laptop".

![Setup, dark](https://github.com/Snooper42/homelab-wizard/raw/claude/homelab-0-14-continue-telwyj/docs/images/app-setup-dark.png)

**Setup only while something needs you.** Setup is in the sidebar only while one of these holds:
- a step is left (or one that can wait);
- a homelab update is waiting;
- the runtime or the homelab folder is missing;
- a job's results are still on it;
- it is the screen shown.

Once every step is done, it leaves the sidebar. ⌘4 (Ctrl+4) and the sidebar's **● Update ready** still open it, and it comes back by itself when a step comes undone. The steps are now read at start whatever screen opens, so this holds on Status too (`setupNav` in `screens/setup.ts`).

**Unplugging a laptop is not a step coming undone.** The laptop step ("This laptop stays plugged in and open") is done while keeping it awake is on, plugged in or not (`internal/setup`; `TestLaptopStep`). Turning keeping awake off still undoes it, and Status' line says when it is on battery.

**How this machine looks after the homelab.**
- `App.Health` (`app/health.go`) reports:
  - the agent: running (its engine answers, `engine.Dial`), stopped, stopped by Quit (`stopped.json`), or not set up;
  - the watchdog's last check;
  - the power: on battery or plugged in (`battery.Power`), and whether it is kept awake (`KEEP_AWAKE`).
- Setup draws this as four tiles (agent, runtime, power, disk), with **Start it** for a stopped agent (`App.StartAgent` = `homelab resume`, its words in `scripts/logs/resume.log`).
- Status keeps the same facts as one line at its top (`#healthLine`).

**Finish setting up** (`setup/Checklist.tsx`):
- one line per step, grouped as **Needs you**, **Can wait** (folded, `#toggleLater`) and **Done** (folded, `#toggleDone`);
- each step opens with its chevron for the rest of what it says;
- **Do the N I can do for you**;
- once all are done, a single line: "All N steps are done".

**The update card in plain words** (`setup/Upgrade.tsx`):
- "An update is ready: N changes", with the changes' titles without their PR numbers;
- what it does, with no `origin/main` or `.env`;
- **Release notes (N)** in place of "What is new (N)".

**Settings › This Mac** (This PC, This machine) now holds:
- the machine's details (`#hostInfo`: the machine, the runtime, what runs in the background, the menu bar item or tray icon, the app menu, the homelab folder, the disks, the version and Go back);
- **Make a diagnostics report**, with its log under the button. A crash note's **Send the report** goes there.

**Go back** opens Setup, where its progress shows.

Docs:
- CHANGELOG ([Unreleased]: New and Improved);
- app/README;
- where the report and the disks are now: Getting Started, Testing, Troubleshooting, Known Issues, Host.

Docs screenshots retaken (Setup, first run, update, Status, Settings).

## Safety impact

- [x] Does not expose an app to the internet by default
- [x] Does not write secrets anywhere but `.env` (mode 0600), nor print them
- [x] Does not delete data without a backup and a confirmation first
- [x] Does not claim it works on a machine unless it was actually tried there

## Validation

- [x] `go vet ./...` and `go test ./...` (new: `TestAgentState`, `TestHealth`; `TestLaptopStep` for the unplugged laptop; `TestResumeKeepsWhatItSaid` checks that resume's error carries what it said)
- [x] `go run ./cmd/homelab validate`, and `go run ./cmd/homelab docs --check` ("docs are up to date")
- [x] `make check app-check frontend-check app-smoke`: locally `make check`, `make coverage` (app 73.5%, floor 73%), `make app-check`, `make frontend-check`, gosec on the app module, and the full click-through in light (362 ok, no FAIL). CI on cf219a9 (https://github.com/Snooper42/homelab-wizard/actions/runs/40810956155): check, app, security, test (macos-latest), test (windows-latest), smoke (light) and smoke (dark) all green. Each smoke log runs to its last screen (`ok   The phone, Backups, Mac, yellow accent, light, more contrast`, and the dark one) with 362 ok and no FAIL, including the six new checks:
  - Setup leaves the sidebar once nothing needs you;
  - Setup stays in the sidebar while a step is left;
  - Setup's tiles: a stopped agent says so, and Start it starts it;
  - Status keeps this machine's line;
  - Finish setting up: what can wait folds, and a step opens for the rest;
  - the diagnostics report, from Settings › This Mac.
- [ ] Tried on a machine, if it changes what runs (docs/Testing.md has the steps): the owner looks at it on their Mac in the next build

Merge only on the owner's go-ahead.

